## Attack count, charge and button routing

Support 2–5 sequential numbered attack families. Ground and air versions are one family. Charge replacements count toward this total. Preserve this document's existing decision that extra_attack is separate from the numbered limit; shield, movement, jump, charge and transform are also not numbered attacks.

Every independently accessible numbered attack must have an explicit, functional midair_attackN definition and animation. Only charge-exclusive attacks are exempt. An independent attack5 always needs midair_attack5. Do not satisfy validation with an idle pose, a missing clip or a silent ground-only fallback. Keep extra_attack's existing character-specific air/ground restrictions unless separately redesigned.

All currently shipped characters should retain Charge. Also support a genuinely charge-disabled character, as required by the no-charge examples. Model charge availability separately from whether chargeReplacements is empty: a charge-capable two-attack character can have no replacements. Add an explicit per-character capability if the current schema cannot express that distinction, and route controls, AI and state transitions through it.

| Numbered attacks | Charge routing enabled | Independent numbered buttons | Charge substitutions |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 2 | No | attack1, attack2 | None |
| 3 | No | attack1, attack2, attack3 | None |
| 4 | No | attack1, attack2, attack3, attack4 | None |
| 5 | No | attack1, attack2, attack3, attack4, attack5 | None |
| 2 | Yes | attack1, attack2 | None |
| 3 | Yes | attack1, attack2 | attack1 -> attack3 |
| 4 | Yes | attack1, attack2 | attack1 -> attack3; attack2 -> attack4 |
| 5 | Yes | attack1, attack2, attack5 | attack1 -> attack3; attack2 -> attack4 |

For the five-attack charged loadout, the third numbered button still sends attack5, not attack3. Substitutions change the move selected by an existing button; they must not create duplicate buttons or renumber the move IDs.

A charge-disabled fighter must not enter the charge stance, receive charge-only regeneration bonuses, expose an unusable Charge action, or have AI attempt it. Preserve separate downward-input uses such as fast fall, platform interactions and launch steering when disabling the charge ability.

Use a shared, data-driven loadout resolver for combat, controllers, AI, button visibility and labels. Validate unknown IDs, gaps, more than five families, missing required air variants, missing objects and illegal or duplicate routes. Charge-exclusive attacks must not also be reachable through their own keyboard/gamepad/touch button.

Keep the existing charge input timing, buffering, cooldown consumption, release/repress requirement, cancellation and interruption semantics. Verify that a cooldown cannot be bypassed by sending a different button or changing state. A replacement on cooldown must not accidentally execute its base attack; preserve separately documented fallback behavior for unavailable targets or art.

## Attack-created objects and existing mechanics

Every projectile, clone, summon, deployable or attack-owned effect uses its owning attack's object namespace. Air-specific objects use midair_attackN_object when owned by that air move. Runtime instance IDs may distinguish concurrent entities; they must not alter the asset frame suffix.

Preserve specialized projectile, summon and technique behavior classes. The naming requirement does not require deleting those abstractions or turning every entity into a generic projectile. If an attack creates several visually distinct objects, define collision-free child keys beneath its object namespace and document that extension; never reuse the final frame number as an object-type discriminator.

For character 0001, preserve:

- attack1 and midair_attack1: the existing punch and airborne slash.
- attack2 and midair_attack2: the existing kick/launcher and airborne downward attack.
- attack3: the clone summon reached through Charge + attack1. Its appearance/disappearance cloud uses attack3_object. Preserve reversed disappearance playback and the clone's explicit reuse of the owner's attack1 or midair_attack2 clips and hit data.
- attack4: the Sphere Rush reached through Charge + attack2. Preserve all form, rush, confirm, explosion, recovery and whiff phases; the 12 pose frames and 11 object frames; hand offsets; target binding; tick damage; explosion timing; interrupts and cooldown.
- extra_attack: the shuriken throw, with its object release timing, flight, hitbox, lifetime and animation.

A summon that reuses owner poses need not duplicate the PNGs to rename their pixels. Keep that reuse explicit in its definition while naming summon-owned objects and effects after attack3.

